# The audit card is a list of stamps, one a line, that several people add
# to on different branches. Keeping both sides' lines means nobody has a
# conflict to settle by hand. A file keeps one stamp, so where two
# branches stamped the same file the merge leaves two lines for it, and
# `scripts/audit-stamp.py check` fails in the pre-commit hooks and in CI
# until the file is stamped again.
audit/ledger.tsv merge=union
